# order — the system's files, in the order the interpreter compiles them. A file that is not named
# here does not load: Berry resolves a global when it compiles a file, so a class has to be a global
# by the time a file that names it is compiled.
# The browser's Forward opens the settings list, and its rows come from the registry.
browser.be
# The home scene's run, which home.be holds.
home_machine.be
# The device's own settings list, which home.be opens on a held Up.
settings.be
# Last: it names browserScene and open_system_settings in its gestures.
home.be
